00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:58.371
-♪ Truth or Truth ♪

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:02.574
-Alright.

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:05.477
You're up first, Amsters.

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:06.912
What's it gonna be?

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:09.649
Truth...or truth?

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:16.289
-Truth.

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:18.657
[ Clears throat ]

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:22.828
-What's your biggest fear?

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:25.030
-Easy.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.066
Being mistaken for J.Lo.

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:29.135
[ Laughter ]

00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:35.074
And then being asked to dance.

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:37.143
And dancing better than J.Lo.

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.410
[ Laughter ]

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.380
And J.Lo being angry.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.448
-Easy.

00:09:42.448 --> 00:09:43.816
-I don't want J.Lo
to be angry at me.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:44.983
-[ Chuckling ] No.

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:46.152
-That's my biggest fear.

00:09:46.152 --> 00:09:48.420
-Okay.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.622
-Jimmy.
-Mm-hmm.

00:09:50.622 --> 00:09:53.359
-Now it's your turn, I think.

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:54.593
Is this how this works?

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:57.163
-Yeah.

00:09:57.163 --> 00:09:58.831
-Truth or truth?

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:04.436
-Truth.

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:06.472
-[ Clears throat ]

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:12.745
Where's someplace
you've never had sex?

00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:13.779
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:15.748
-In my 20s.

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.583
[ Laughter ]

00:10:17.583 --> 00:10:19.752
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:26.926
Well, I did run into Chuck
in the elevator once.

00:10:27.993 --> 00:10:28.928
-So I've heard.

00:10:28.928 --> 00:10:29.929
-Your turn!

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:32.398
-Fine!

00:10:32.398 --> 00:10:35.867
-Truth or truth?

00:10:35.867 --> 00:10:38.637
-[ Scoffs, laughs ]

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:41.340
Truth.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.043
-What does your real voice
sound like?

00:10:44.043 --> 00:10:46.311
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.311 --> 00:10:53.419
♪♪

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:56.455
-[ Accented lisping ]
What do you mean?

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:59.525
Do you mean when I'm speaking
my native tongue?

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:01.627
[ Laughter ]

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:04.563
Do you mean when I...
speak to my relatives

00:11:04.563 --> 00:11:08.701
or my people I lauve [love]?

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.869
-"Lauve"?

00:11:10.869 --> 00:11:11.937
-Yimmy.

00:11:11.937 --> 00:11:13.739
[ Laughter ]

00:11:13.739 --> 00:11:16.842
-It's Sofía Vergara
or something.

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:18.443
-[ Spits ]
-Oh, my God!

00:11:18.443 --> 00:11:20.312
Sorry, doesn't mean any--
Sorry to say that.

00:11:20.312 --> 00:11:22.415
-How dare you?
-I'm not comparing anything.

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:23.749
You're both --
-We're very different.

00:11:23.749 --> 00:11:24.950
-Different. Very different.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.720
Apologize.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.988
-[ Normal voice ]
Jimmy, it's your turn.

00:11:29.988 --> 00:11:33.892
And I mean, I've enjoyed
this game so far, but...

00:11:33.892 --> 00:11:35.627
I'd like you to tell the truth.

00:11:35.627 --> 00:11:38.163
Truth or truth?

00:11:38.163 --> 00:11:41.033
-Okay, truth.

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.235
-What's in your pocket
right now?

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:47.773
[ Laughter ]

00:11:49.541 --> 00:11:52.911
-A CD case of Bon Jovi's
2005 album "Have a Nice Day,"

00:11:52.911 --> 00:11:55.581
but inside is Green Day's
"Dookie" CD.

00:11:55.581 --> 00:11:57.750
[ Laughter ]

00:12:00.618 --> 00:12:02.921
-Want me to prove it?

00:12:02.921 --> 00:12:04.923
[ Laughs ]

00:12:04.923 --> 00:12:07.926
Check this out, man.

00:12:07.926 --> 00:12:11.163
Bang.
-Whoa.

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:12.131
-Bang.

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:13.599
That's "Dookie" right there.

00:12:13.599 --> 00:12:15.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:18.671 --> 00:12:20.639
Alright, last one, Poehler!

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:22.240
-Both great songs.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.676
-[ Laughs ] Truth --

00:12:24.676 --> 00:12:26.612
Truth or truth?

00:12:26.612 --> 00:12:28.480
Or truth.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.748
-[ Sighs ]

00:12:29.748 --> 00:12:32.184
I'm too old for dares.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:34.887
I'm too smart for lies.

00:12:34.887 --> 00:12:36.255
I'm too quick --

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:37.856
-Don't read your lower back
tattoo.

00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:38.924
Just --

00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:40.192
[ Laughter ]

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:42.627
Just say truth or truth.
-You're right, you're right.

00:12:42.627 --> 00:12:44.630
I shouldn't say my tattoo,
I should live it.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.864
You're right.

00:12:45.864 --> 00:12:48.533
-[ Laughs ]
-I just -- I love it.

00:12:48.533 --> 00:12:50.669
-"I shouldn't say my tattoo,
I should live it."

00:12:50.669 --> 00:12:52.037
That's correct.
-Okay, truth.

00:12:52.037 --> 00:12:53.872
-[ Laughs ]

00:12:53.872 --> 00:12:56.175
Ah.

00:12:56.175 --> 00:12:58.377
What's your Gmail password?

00:13:01.513 --> 00:13:05.451
-PizzaHutMonkeyButt.orgy.

00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:07.453
-[ Laughs ]

00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:09.721
That is Truth or Truth.

00:13:09.721 --> 00:13:11.523
Our thanks to Amy Poehler!

00:13:11.523 --> 00:13:13.525
-My little guy
is still afraid of movies.

00:13:13.525 --> 00:13:16.094
He won't go see movies, so --

00:13:16.094 --> 00:13:17.429
-He's 5 now?
-He's 5,

00:13:17.429 --> 00:13:19.365
and he just does a thing of,
like, you know,

00:13:19.365 --> 00:13:21.399
he, like, talks a big game,
and then he's just like,

00:13:21.399 --> 00:13:24.670
"Um, no, thanks."
Like, he just bails.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.072
So when we had a screening of
"Inside Out," actually,

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:28.741
and all of his friends
were there,

00:13:28.741 --> 00:13:31.143
and he just was like,
"I'm just gonna" --

00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:34.180
like, he just pretended like
he had something else to do.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.547
-As a 5-year-old?
-It was super cute, yeah.

00:13:35.547 --> 00:13:37.415
-That's super cute,
and how's the older one?

00:13:37.415 --> 00:13:39.918
-And Archie's
ready for anything.

00:13:39.918 --> 00:13:41.553
In fact, the other day, he --

00:13:41.553 --> 00:13:45.057
I walked by and he was with
some neighbors of ours,

00:13:45.057 --> 00:13:46.191
and I was like,
"What are you doing?"

00:13:46.191 --> 00:13:47.425
He's like,
"Mom, I'm watching Divergent."

00:13:47.425 --> 00:13:49.394
I was like,
"Should you be watching?"

00:13:49.394 --> 00:13:50.428
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:13:50.428 --> 00:13:51.696
Should he be watching
"Divergent"?

00:13:51.696 --> 00:13:53.164
-I don't know it, though.
-It might be too

00:13:53.164 --> 00:13:54.566
something, right? Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:13:54.566 --> 00:13:56.268
-It's violent or something.
I don't even know.

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:58.670
-We're talking about things
we didn't even prep.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:13:59.971
-We don't care.
We don't need 'em.

00:13:59.971 --> 00:14:01.340
I just want to know about
those kids.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.641
Are they best friends?
-They're great.

00:14:02.641 --> 00:14:05.010
They're so great.
Archie's doing this thing now,

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:09.147
though, where he's kind of
acting like, um --

00:14:09.147 --> 00:14:12.451
he's the older brother and he
tortures his younger brother.

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:14.386
So...
-Yeah.

00:14:14.386 --> 00:14:17.089
-...he psychologically
tortures him.

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:19.525
So, he just does really quiet,
like,

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:22.694
Kevin Spacey-like moves

00:14:22.694 --> 00:14:26.164
where he just --
where Abel, my younger one,

00:14:26.164 --> 00:14:28.400
will be like, "I can't wait to,"
you know, "play with my LEGOs,"

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:30.936
and Archie will be like,
"Those aren't your LEGOs."

00:14:30.936 --> 00:14:32.938
[ Laughter ]

00:14:32.938 --> 00:14:35.374
And he'll be like, "They're
mine, they're my LEGOs,"

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:37.776
and he'll be like,
"Not anymore."

00:14:37.776 --> 00:14:40.612
And Abel will just immediately
start to cry, like,

00:14:40.612 --> 00:14:42.213
and Archie will be like,
you know,

00:14:42.213 --> 00:14:44.082
"If you want to play,
you have to talk to me first."

00:14:44.082 --> 00:14:47.319
He's just constantly --
he's just constantly horrible.

00:14:47.319 --> 00:14:48.820
-Yeah.
-He's just always telling him,

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.455
like, up is down and...

00:14:50.455 --> 00:14:52.057
-Yeah, just whatever you can do
psychologically.

00:14:52.057 --> 00:14:54.192
Are they going to see
"Star Wars,"

00:14:54.192 --> 00:14:55.160
the big "Star Wars" movie?

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.463
-Well, I think they like --

00:14:57.463 --> 00:14:59.063
again, they like the idea of it.

00:14:59.063 --> 00:15:00.565
It's a little too
adult for them,

00:15:00.565 --> 00:15:01.733
so I don't think
they're gonna see it,

00:15:01.733 --> 00:15:05.271
but I think -- so no.

00:15:05.271 --> 00:15:07.072
-Yeah.

00:15:07.072 --> 00:15:08.306
They're not gonna see it, no.

00:15:08.306 --> 00:15:09.375
-No.

